# Packages whose ELFs go in indium's initramfs, one per line (AGAST #2759).
#
# The one list. tools/stage_initramfs.sh is its one reader (its header has
# the format), and indium's Makefile (build/initramfs.tar, run-uefi),
# tools/mkiso.sh and harland's boot scripts all stage through it; `#` starts
# a comment. After the package name, optional fields: compiler=
# ritz1_selfhosted builds it in the builder image, bin=SRC[:DEST] stages only
# SRC.elf, as /bin/DEST.
# init's Tier-1 suite spawns binaries from all of these: prism builds
# hello_gfx, rzsh builds /bin/rzsh. projects/ritz/tools/
# test_indium_initramfs_pkgs.py fails if init spawns a /bin/NAME that no
# package here builds.
indium
rzsh
prism
# harland's kernel-spawned programs (RING2_NET.md D4): /bin/netd, the
# network service with the NIC's driver inside it (D9, AGAST #4875), which
# the translating boot spawns (AGAST #4735, #4743).
harland/system
# Buddhafinger, the editor (AGAST #4834, M4 #4792): ritz1_selfhosted only
# (#4813), so built in the builder image; its Harland ELF only (not the Linux
# editor or bench), installed as /bin/buddhafinger. tools/
# test_harland_console.sh (#4833) boots this staged image.
buddhafinger  compiler=ritz1_selfhosted  bin=buddhafinger.harland:buddhafinger
